<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>BACKGROUND</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For clarity, the notations used throughout this paper are summarized in Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ GRNND: A GPU-Parallel Relative NN-Descent Algorithm for Efficient Approximate Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1. </span>Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Approximate Nearest Neighbor Search (ANNS) aims to retrieve vectors close to a query <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> by trading exactness for improved efficiency. A typical ANNS system consists of two stages: index construction and online querying.
Graph-based methods have emerged as one of the most effective approaches due to their superior trade-off between accuracy and efficiency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2021a</a>)</cite>. They are based on a navigable proximity graph, where the quality of the graph largely determines search performance. Sparse graphs with adaptive neighbor sets often support more efficient navigation than uniform <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN graphs, but their construction is computationally costly.
During querying, performance is usually evaluated using two metrics: Recall@k and Queries Per Second (QPS). Recall measures accuracy as the fraction of true nearest neighbors retrieved, while QPS quantifies the number of queries processed per unit of time, indicating the efficiency of the search process.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2. </span>RNN-Descent Algorithm</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> RNN-Descent Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Graph<math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{INITIALIZATION}(v,S,N_{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>INITIALIZATION</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{INITIALIZATION}(v,S,N_{v})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{UPDATE\_NEIGHBORS}(v,R,N_{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>UPDATE_NEIGHBORS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{UPDATE\_NEIGHBORS}(v,R,N_{v})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}\neq T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}\neq T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ADD\_REVERSE\_EDGES}(v,R,N_{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>ADD_REVERSE_EDGES</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ADD\_REVERSE\_EDGES}(v,R,N_{v})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">RNN-Descent begins with a randomly initialized <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>-NN index and iteratively refines the graph by applying the RNG criterion. For a vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with two candidate neighbors <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, both neighbors are retained only if:</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d(n_{1},v)&lt;d(n_{1},n_{2})\land d(n_{2},v)&lt;d(n_{1},n_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d(n_{1},v)&lt;d(n_{1},n_{2})\land d(n_{2},v)&lt;d(n_{1},n_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In other words, if <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are closer to each other than either is to <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, then the edge between them takes precedence over their connections to <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>. As shown in Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.2. RNN-Descent Algorithm ‣ 2. BACKGROUND ‣ GRNND: A GPU-Parallel Relative NN-Descent Algorithm for Efficient Approximate Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is initially connected to two neighbors <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is closer to <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> than to <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, the edge between <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is removed and replaced by an edge between <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02774v1/RNG_strategy.svg" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/157;" width="452" height="157" aria-label="Three subfigures illustrating the refinement of a neighbor graph using the Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) strategy. Subfigure (a) shows the initial graph before the neighbor update. Subfigure (b) highlights the edge selection process based on the RNG criterion, where an edge is retained only if no closer common neighbor exists. Subfigure (c) presents the updated graph after applying the RNG strategy, with spurious edges removed to improve graph quality."><p>Three subfigures illustrating the refinement of a neighbor graph using the Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) strategy. Subfigure (a) shows the initial graph before the neighbor update. Subfigure (b) highlights the edge selection process based on the RNG criterion, where an edge is retained only if no closer common neighbor exists. Subfigure (c) presents the updated graph after applying the RNG strategy, with spurious edges removed to improve graph quality.</p></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>. </span><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Neighbor refinement of vertex <math id="S2.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> under the RNG criterion. (a) Initial candidate neighbors; (b) RNG-based edge pruning; (c) Refined neighbor set of <math id="S2.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span><span id="acmlabel1" class="ltx_acm_description ltx_centering ltx_nodisplay">Three subfigures illustrating the refinement of a neighbor graph using the Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) strategy. Subfigure (a) shows the initial graph before the neighbor update. Subfigure (b) highlights the edge selection process based on the RNG criterion, where an edge is retained only if no closer common neighbor exists. Subfigure (c) presents the updated graph after applying the RNG strategy, with spurious edges removed to improve graph quality.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The complete algorithm is presented in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 2.2. RNN-Descent Algorithm ‣ 2. BACKGROUND ‣ GRNND: A GPU-Parallel Relative NN-Descent Algorithm for Efficient Approximate Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and consists of three key steps: (1) random initialization of neighbor pools (line 3), (2) iterative refinement based on the RNG criterion (line 6), and (3) insertion of reverse edges to maintain structural diversity and avoid premature convergence (line 9).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Each vertex sequentially refines its candidate list <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, as detailed in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 2.2. RNN-Descent Algorithm ‣ 2. BACKGROUND ‣ GRNND: A GPU-Parallel Relative NN-Descent Algorithm for Efficient Approximate Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. First, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is sorted by ascending distance <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v,n)</annotation></semantics></math> and duplicates are removed (line 3). The first neighbor (i.e., closest) is always accepted and added to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each subsequent candidate <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> (line 5) is compared with all previously accepted neighbors <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\prime}\in N_{v}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\prime}\in N_{v}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (line 7).
If any <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(n,n^{\prime})\leq d(v,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(n,n^{\prime})\leq d(v,n)</annotation></semantics></math> (line 8), <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is excluded from <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and redirected to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{n^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{n^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (lines 9–11). Otherwise, <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is retained and added to <math id="S2.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (line 15).</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> UPDATE_NEIGHBORS</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, candidate neighbors <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> Refined neighbors <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             Sort <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> by ascending <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(v,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(v,n)</annotation></semantics></math> and remove duplicates

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
             Retain top <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> closest candidates in <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in N_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in N_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
