<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="S4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance under different candidate update strategies on GRNND across datasets: ascending may cause convergence traps, descending improves exploration but is costly, while random provides a balanced trade-off.</span><span id="acmlabel7" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">Performance under different sampling parameters during the process of adding reverse edges.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
