<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>. </span><span id="S4.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance under different back-edge Sampling ratio (<math id="S4.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>)s (reverse edges added) on GRNND across datasets: low ratios speed up but reduce accuracy, high ratios improve quality but slow down, while around 0.6 offers the best trade-off.</span><span id="acmlabel8" class="ltx_nodisplay ltx_acm_description">Performance under different sampling parameters during the process of adding reverse edges.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
